      "description": "Watch Miami FC vs Tampa Bay Rowdies highlights and goals from USL Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 25, 2026. The USL Championship clash between Miami FC and Tampa Bay Rowdies promised to be a showcase of tactical discipline and competitive fire. Both sides entered the match seeking to assert their dominance in a fixture that has historically delivered high drama. Escalation in the Second Half On July 25, 2026 , the contest reached a boiling point as the match entered its final phase. The physicality of the encounter was evident early on, but the referee was forced to take control in the 72nd minute, issuing a yellow card to Jürgen Locadia . This caution served as the catalyst for a frantic period of play, where the momentum shifted rapidly between the two Florida rivals. Locadia Finds the Net but Rowdies React Miami FC found a lifeline in the 76th minute when Jürgen Locadia turned from a cautioned player into a goalscorer. Assisted by a sharp pass from M. Ndongo , Locadia leveled the score at 2-2, sending the home crowd into raptures. However, the parity lasted only four minutes. In the 80th minute, the Tampa Bay Rowdies struck back decisively. Marco Micaletto found the back of the net following an assist from C. Ostrem , restoring the visitors' lead at 3-2. A Disciplinary Struggle in Stoppage Time As Miami FC pushed for another equalizer, the game became increasingly fractured. Yellow cards were shown to Miami's D. Mello and M. Ndongo as tensions flared. The final moments were characterized by a defensive stand from the Rowdies , which came at a cost of multiple bookings. In the dying seconds of stoppage time, N. Dossantos , J. Waite , and match-winner Marco Micaletto all received yellow cards. Despite the late disciplinary chaos, Tampa Bay held their nerve to secure all three points."
